  "R3_sign": "the direction holds iff at least 60% of start dates move the same way (threshold frozen before the first run)",
  "R4_calendar": "the start-date term is the interquartile spread of the paired deltas; if it is at least as large as the median, the cadence gap lives inside the start-date noise",
  "R5_window": "TO_CUTOFF anchors are nested (all books end at the same cutoff); the fixed 252/504-bar rulers slice each run's own head and are the ones allowed to speak about a single year of holding. A start too short for a horizon is a named hole for that horizon only",
